{"ref":"BDB, פְּדָיָהוּ","hw":"פְּדָיָהוּ","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">פְּדָיָהוּ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">פְּדָיָה</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. (</strong><span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <em>hath ransomed;</em> in late Bab. <em>Padâma</em>, Hilpr<sup>Univ. Pa. Exp. ix. 27, 68</sup><strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">פְּדָיָה</span>:<br><strong>1.</strong>  father-in-law of Josiah <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:36\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.36\">2 K 23:36</a>, but 𝔊 Εδειλ (𝔊L Ιερεμιας, from v <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:31\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.31\">31</a>).<br><strong>2.</strong>  father of Zerub. <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 3:18\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.3.18\">1 Ch 3:18</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 3:19\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.3.19\">19</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong> <strong>a.</strong>  <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 3:25\" href=\"/Nehemiah.3.25\">Ne 3:25</a>. <strong>b.</strong>  <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 8:4\" href=\"/Nehemiah.8.4\">8:4</a>.<br><strong>4.</strong>  Benjamite <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 11:7\" href=\"/Nehemiah.11.7\">Ne 11:7</a>.<br><strong>5.</strong>  Levite <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 13:13\" href=\"/Nehemiah.13.13\">Ne 13:13</a>.<br><strong>6.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">פְּדָיָהוּ</span>, Manassite <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 27:20\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.27.20\">1 Ch 27:20</a>—𝔊 (except <strong>1</strong>) Φα(λ)δαιας, etc.","next":"BDB, יִפְדְּיָה","prev":"BDB, פְּדָהצוּר"}